# Wyrd project rules

## What Wyrd is
An AI game master that can't cheat. Muse Spark narrates; a TypeScript rule engine is the only thing allowed to change game state. Hidden secrets are sealed with a SHA-256 hash at game start and revealed at the end.

## Structure
- server/ : Node 24 + TypeScript + Express (ESM)
  - server/src/game/ : pure game logic (types, state, rules, worlds). No network calls, no Express.
  - server/src/ai/ : Muse Spark calls and the tool-calling loop
  - server/src/http/ : Express routes
- web/ : React + Vite + TypeScript (later)
- scripts/ : one-off API test scripts. Do not modify.

## Hard rules
1. Only functions in server/src/game/rules.ts may change GameState. Everything else treats state as read-only.
2. Never read or print .env. Use process.env.META_API_KEY on the server only.
3. Never put API keys or API calls in web/.
4. Always set the model explicitly: muse-spark-1.3.
5. Game logic takes randomness as an injected function (rng) so tests can control it.
6. Every rule function has vitest unit tests covering valid and invalid cases.
7. Strict TypeScript. No `any`.
8. Only change the files the task names. No unrelated refactors. No new dependencies unless the task allows them.
9. Do not run git commands. The developer commits.
10. Any frontend work must follow docs/UI_STYLE.md (the V3 "Kinetic fate" style).

## Commands
- cd server; npm test
- cd server; npx tsc --noEmit
- The terminal is Windows PowerShell 5.1: chain commands with ; not &&